{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/959049-advice-on-my-first-beast","id":959049,"title":"Advice on my first Beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-27T20:29:02-07:00","id":959049,"title":"Advice on my first Beast","content":"Just want an opinion on my first beast and would appreciate the feedback. The premises for this beast is an Eshmaki Collector who loves to take from people what they covet most, and also through doing so teaches a person appreciation for what they have.<br /> <br /> Here are stats I also got a bonus 11xp from previous char death it is a crossover<br /> The theme is a naga-esque lurker that hunts its prey stealthy only to strike viciously like a snake, its lair follows a kind of marsh and heavy rain feel. With the lair traits Downpour, Suffocating, Flooding as starts.<br /> <br /> Lair 3 dots<br /> <br /> Mental- Intel 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> Physical- Strength 2, Dex 3, Stamina 3<br /> Social- Pres 2, Manip 1, Comp 3<br /> <br /> Skills<br /> <br /> Mental Skills- Academics 1, Invest 2, Occult 3, Medicine 2<br /> Physical Skills- Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Survival 1<br /> Social Skills- Empathy 1, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 1<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> Fighting Finesse(Dexterity)<br /> Iron Skin 2 dots<br /> Killer Instinct 2 dots<br /> Indomitable<br /> Skill Specialty(Brawling)<br /> <br /> Atavism<br /> <br /> Relentless Hunter [Eshmaki]<br /> Heart of the Ocean [Makara]<br /> From the Shadows [Eshmaki]<br /> Limb From Limb [Eshmaki]<br /> <br /> Nightmares<br /> <br /> You Cannot Run<br /> Behold, My True Form!<br /> <br /> <br /> Any advice for on how to improve concept, or overall tips on improving said character would be helpful also please keep in mind this is my first beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:01:48-07:00","id":959067,"title":"","content":"Slight thing, you may want to specify more on what your Beast collects. Mostly for when you're at higher satiety and if you're in a mixed game you'll be able to feed more often from Family Dinners, but at that point you'll need something more specific than just a person's most treasured possession.(Though you can specify it down from a very specific type of person as easily as a specific type of object. The main part is that it is supposed to become harder to find the food to feed your Horror as it gets more picky and well fed.)<br /> <br /> You'll need to adjust your skill specialty. It needs to be something your character does with Brawling not just brawling. Like is your character an unarmed brawler to simulate just rising from the water and lashing at the target, a grappler who immobilizes it's prey then does what it wants, or are you going with the cunning snake thing and specializing in improvised weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:09:57-07:00","id":959073,"title":"","content":"Ok I like the idea of Grappling and dragging someone down to suffocate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:12:16-07:00","id":959074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/959049-advice-on-my-first-beast?p=959067#post959067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight thing, you may want to specify more on what your Beast collects. Mostly for when you're at higher satiety and if you're in a mixed game you'll be able to feed more often from Family Dinners, but at that point you'll need something more specific than just a person's most treasured possession.(Though you can specify it down from a very specific type of person as easily as a specific type of object. The main part is that it is supposed to become harder to find the food to feed your Horror as it gets more picky and well fed.)<br /> <br /> You'll need to adjust your skill specialty. It needs to be something your character does with Brawling not just brawling. Like is your character an unarmed brawler to simulate just rising from the water and lashing at the target, a grappler who immobilizes it's prey then does what it wants, or are you going with the cunning snake thing and specializing in improvised weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you think would be a fun thing to collect, I was thinking originally Valuables such as jewelery or maybe peoples loved ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:48:45-07:00","id":959086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/959049-advice-on-my-first-beast?p=959074#post959074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think would be a fun thing to collect, I was thinking originally Valuables such as jewelery or maybe peoples loved ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh loved ones are fun. However if we look at the Mahabarata for so information on Nagas it says nagas were :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the snakes were of virulent poison, great prowess and excess of strength, and ever bent on biting other creatures&quot; </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Actually I like this idea. How lethal are you planning to go with this? Like is your Beast planning to often leave survivors (generally not trying to kill anyone, but if the crap hits the fan) or is your Beast more than willing to end someone when they go to feed? Cause if you're going lethal then the idea collecting a person's loved one's can be something like ambushing the target hitting them with Basilisk's Touch (I would advise that over limb from limb actually) Then taking a picture of the deceased and the one mourner or an important object from both of them. <br /> In a nonlethal iteration I'm fond of claiming the targets as a hostage and exchanging them for blackmail material or things of great personal significance in exchange for the hostage. This is assuming you don't just go with the idea of say taking the person down walking out with their wallet and phone and IDs. <br /> <br /> In these case your horror's scale would be driving you to more difficult targets higher up in a specific field. So like your low feeding is anyone maybe you start having to target people holding greater power in the community as it goes higher, and eventually you'll need to hit the mayor/prince/whatever criminal runs the town from the shadows. <br /> <br /> Thoughts, comments, other ideas? Can you give me some more information on how you want to run this Beast? Any idea what the others in the group are? It doesn't hurt if your Beast started hanging with them because you got along and favored the same hunting grounds.</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:07:28-07:00","id":959092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/959049-advice-on-my-first-beast?p=959086#post959086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh loved ones are fun. However if we look at the Mahabarata for so information on Nagas it says nagas were :<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Actually I like this idea. How lethal are you planning to go with this? Like is your Beast planning to often leave survivors (generally not trying to kill anyone, but if the crap hits the fan) or is your Beast more than willing to end someone when they go to feed? Cause if you're going lethal then the idea collecting a person's loved one's can be something like ambushing the target hitting them with Basilisk's Touch (I would advise that over limb from limb actually) Then taking a picture of the deceased and the one mourner or an important object from both of them.<br /> In a nonlethal iteration I'm fond of claiming the targets as a hostage and exchanging them for blackmail material or things of great personal significance in exchange for the hostage. This is assuming you don't just go with the idea of say taking the person down walking out with their wallet and phone and IDs.<br /> <br /> In these case your horror's scale would be driving you to more difficult targets higher up in a specific field. So like your low feeding is anyone maybe you start having to target people holding greater power in the community as it goes higher, and eventually you'll need to hit the mayor/prince/whatever criminal runs the town from the shadows.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, comments, other ideas? Can you give me some more information on how you want to run this Beast? Any idea what the others in the group are? It doesn't hurt if your Beast started hanging with them because you got along and favored the same hunting grounds.</span>[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'll be hanging with mages for the most part, and i'm wanting my beast to be able to stealthy stalk my prey and a thought i've considered is after taking a love one bring them back to my lair for sport. For you never know what you appreciate until it's gone. <br /> <br /> On running the beast I want her to be much more quiet with life being shy, but her horror is relentless in it's pursuit. I see my beast as the kind to go out and about and to observe people, loved ones interacting and taking from them something meaningful, or the loved ones themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:22:13-07:00","id":959099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/959049-advice-on-my-first-beast?p=959092#post959092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'll be hanging with mages for the most part, and i'm wanting my beast to be able to stealthy stalk my prey and a thought i've considered is after taking a love one bring them back to my lair for sport. For you never know what you appreciate until it's gone.<br /> <br /> On running the beast I want her to be much more quiet with life being shy, but her horror is relentless in it's pursuit. I see my beast as the kind to go out and about and to observe people, loved ones interacting and taking from them something meaningful, or the loved ones themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so are you thinking that your character grabs these people and some of the chambers are just populated by the wandering souls that make up the collection, or you thinking the collected individuals are kept in various forms of cages throughout the lair?<br /> <br /> Addendum: Also if you're considering the idea of claiming these people because the other party doesn't appreciate them enough, might I recommend considering a nemesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:27:22-07:00","id":959100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/959049-advice-on-my-first-beast?p=959099#post959099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so are you thinking that your character grabs these people and some of the chambers are just populated by the wandering souls that make up the collection, or you thinking the collected individuals are kept in various forms of cages throughout the lair?<br /> <br /> Addendum: Also if you're considering the idea of claiming these people because the other party doesn't appreciate them enough, might I recommend considering a nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well I was thinking once taken, can be an entertaining form of sport for me or my horror to have some fun, meanwhile the one I lfet behind will now cherish what he has. The state of whoever I take I would write up to they'll prob be dead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:47:41-07:00","id":959109,"title":"","content":"Okay, might I recommend a crypt or a mausoleum as a chamber in the lair where the deceased members of your Beast's collection are stored and functions as the eventual resting place for those who've ceased being able to escape. (Nagas do have some relation to the underworld, plus crypt in the swamp sounds kind of creepy.)<br /> <br /> Still preferring Basilisk's Touch to Limb from Limb as a starting atavism. It functions off touch, so grappling will work well with it and it compliments venomous swamp monster.<br /> <br /> I kind of lean towards You Must Obey over Behold the True Form since your character is a studious one the idea of being able to pry the information from people or make them follow despite their own will seems useful. Plus I will admit a fondness for the thematic idea of robbing a person of their will being done by a being in some versions of the legends known for being a keeper of the powers of consciousness. Granted you don't have to, but I would recommend picking it up later on as it'll be a great tool in your arsenal and probably be of a lot of help to your mage friends too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T23:04:46-07:00","id":959112,"title":"","content":"I like that, I really do, maybe the heart of the lair is like a crypt that has been partially flood, the ceiling seems to be dripping in like rain, and at the center lies the coffins of the belevod and in the very center just a mound of there postions my horror has in order to appreciate things like wedding rings or family necklaces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}